  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-01-29T03:45:40.133Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Bottom Line Up Front:\nPlease allow world authors to append additional volume channels in the player audio menu. This feature could be as simple as going to the VRC Spacialization script on an audio source to use a textbox for what the channel should be named and/or which channel the audio source will be manipulated by. If this textbox is left blank, only the master volume for world audio should effect it.\nReasoning:\nAs is, multiple times there's a hunt for where in a world there is a volume slider *if there is one* for any particular type of audio source. There's a tremendous lack of standards for being able to separately change ambient, music, and video player volumes in worlds. It would bring a tremendous Quality of Life change to VRChat, especially for worlds with a combination of audio that is and isn't centralized. \nFor reference, nearly every VKet and thousands of worlds that use video players for global background music. Would be nice to hear some audio more clearly or lower specific volumes without outright muting everything else from anywhere in large or complex worlds.",
